Feature: Load and Transform Data into f_invntry_bal_dly_hist Table

  Background:
    Given the source tables are available in the purgo_playground schema
    And the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table is empty
    And the current date is set to "20230427"

  Scenario: Successfully load a complete and valid record
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_          | "ITEM001"                |
      | location_code     | "LOC001"                 |
      | posting_date      | "2023-04-26"              |
      | serial_no_        | "SN001"                  |
      | lot_no_           | "LOT001"                 |
      | Expiration_Date   | "2024-04-26"              |
      | Posting_Date      | "2023-04-25"              |
    And a corresponding record in sap_master_data with:
      | Item_No_          | "ITEM001"                |
      | no_               | "NO001"                  |
    And a corresponding record in reservation_entry with:
      | Item_No_          | "ITEM001"                |
      | location_code     | "LOC001"                 |
      | reservation_status | "0"                    |
      | source_type       | "37"                     |
    And a corresponding record in item_qty_on_hand with:
      | Item_No_          | "ITEM001"                |
      | location_code     | "LOC001"                 |
      | qty_on_hand       | "100.0"                  |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should have a record with:
      | co_key                     | "nav_ger1050"                                       |
      | g_account                  | "SAP12345"                                          |
      | g_assignment_type          | "Account"                                           |
      | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd      | "20230427"                                           |
      | g_company_cd               | "1050"                                              |
      | g_company_currency_cd      | "EUR"                                               |
      | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd         | "20240426"                                           |
      | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd   | "99991231"                                           |
      | g_item_nbr                 | "ITEM001"                                           |
      | g_location_cd              | "LOC001"                                            |
      | g_location_status_cd       | "none"                                              |
      | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd| "19000101"                                          |
      | g_lot_nbr                  | "LOT001"                                            |
      | g_lot_status_cd            | "none"                                              |
      | g_plant_cd                 | "CAGER"                                             |
      | g_qty_allocated            | "50.0"                                              |
      | g_qty_available            | "100.0"                                             |
      | g_qty_financial_nettable   | "100.0"                                             |
      | g_qty_in_transit           | null                                                |
      | g_qty_mrp_nettable         | "100.0"                                             |
      | g_qty_on_hand              | "100.0"                                             |
      | g_qty_shippable            | "100.0"                                             |
      | g_source_system_cd         | "nav_ger"                                           |
      | g_unit_cost_company_currency | "20.0"                                           |
      | plant_key                  | "nav_gerCAGER"                                      |
      | plant_location_key         | "nav_gerCAGERLOC001"                                |
      | prod_key                   | "nav_gerITEM001"                                    |
      | prod_plant_key             | "nav_gerITEM001CAGER"                               |
      | prod_plant_location_key    | "nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOC001"                         |
      | prod_plant_lot_key         | "nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOT001"                         |
      | prod_plant_lot_location_key| "nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOT001LOC001"                   |

  Scenario Outline: Load record with missing optional fields and apply default values
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_        | "<item_no_>"            |
      | location_code   | "<location_code>"       |
      | posting_date    | "<posting_date>"        |
      | serial_no_      | "<serial_no_>"          |
      | lot_no_         | "<lot_no_>"             |
      | Expiration_Date | "<expiration_date>"     |
      | Posting_Date    | "<posting_date_alt>"    |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should have a record with:
      | g_assignment_type    | "Account"                        |
      | g_company_cd         | "1050"                           |
      | g_company_currency_cd| "EUR"                            |
      | g_location_status_cd | "none"                           |
      | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd | "19000101"                |
      | g_lot_status_cd      | "none"                           |
      | g_plant_cd           | "CAGER"                          |
      | g_source_system_cd   | "nav_ger"                        |

    Examples:
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date | serial_no_ | lot_no_ | expiration_date | posting_date_alt |
      | ITEM002  | LOC002        | 2023-05-01   | SN002     | LOT002  | 2025-05-01       | 2023-04-30        |
      | ITEM003  | LOC003        | 2023-06-01   |           |        |                   | 2023-06-01        |

  Scenario Outline: Validate mandatory fields completeness and format
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_        | "<item_no_>"            |
      | location_code   | "<location_code>"       |
      | posting_date    | "<posting_date>"        |
      | serial_no_      | "<serial_no_>"          |
      | lot_no_         | "<lot_no_>"             |
      | Expiration_Date | "<expiration_date>"     |
      | Posting_Date    | "<posting_date_alt>"    |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the SQL logic should validate:
      | Field               | Validation Rule                                     | Expected Result          |
      | g_account           | Must be 100% complete and alphanumeric              | "Valid"                  |
      | g_item_nbr          | Must be unique and alphanumeric                     | "Valid"                  |
      | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd | Must be in YYYYMMDD format                      | "Valid"                  |
      | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd  | Must be in YYYYMMDD format or default              | "Valid or Default"       |
      | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd | Must be in YYYYMMDD format or default        | "Valid or Default"       |

    Examples:
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date | serial_no_ | lot_no_ | expiration_date | posting_date_alt |
      |          | LOC004        | 2023-07-01   | SN004     | LOT004  | 2026-07-01       | 2023-07-01        |
      | ITEM005  |               | 2023-08-01   | SN005     | LOT005  | 2027-08-01       | 2023-08-01        |
      | ITEM006  | LOC006        | invalid-date | SN006     | LOT006  | 2028-09-01       | 2023-09-01        |

  Scenario: Handle invalid alphanumeric data in mandatory fields
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_        | "ITEM@007"              |
      | location_code   | "LOC007"                |
      | posting_date    | "2023-09-01"            |
      | serial_no_      | "SN007"                 |
      | lot_no_         | "LOT007"                |
      | Expiration_Date | "2029-09-01"            |
      | Posting_Date    | "2023-09-01"            |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the SQL logic should raise an error:
      | Field      | Error Message                     |
      | g_account  | "g_account must be alphanumeric"  |

  Scenario: Apply concatenation logic for composite keys
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav"                   |
      | g_company_cd     | "1050"                  |
      | g_plant_cd       | "CAGER"                 |
      | g_location_cd    | "LOC008"                |
      | g_item_nbr       | "ITEM008"               |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should have:
      | co_key                     | "nav1050"                                       |
      | plant_key                  | "navCAGER"                                      |
      | plant_location_key         | "navCAGERLOC008"                                |
      | prod_key                   | "navITEM008"                                    |
      | prod_plant_key             | "navITEM008CAGER"                               |
      | prod_plant_location_key    | "navITEM008CAGERLOC008"                         |
      | prod_plant_lot_key         | "navITEM008CAGERnone"                            |
      | prod_plant_lot_location_key| "navITEM008CAGERnoneLOC008"                      |

  Scenario: Maintain snapshot schedule correctly
    Given the current date is "2024-04-27"
    And the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table has records with g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd within:
      | Daily | Weekly | Monthly |
      | 100   | 156    | 60      |
    When the SQL snapshot maintenance runs
    Then the table should retain:
      | Daily | Weekly | Monthly |
      | 100   | 156    | 60      |
      And remove any records older than the defined retention periods

  Scenario Outline: Validate conditional population of quantity fields
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_      | "<item_no_>"          |
      | location_code | "<location_code>"     |
      | qty_on_hand   | "<qty_on_hand>"       |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should have:
      | g_qty_allocated      | "<qty_allocated>"   |
      | g_qty_available      | "<qty_available>"   |
      | g_qty_financial_nettable | "<qty_fin_net>" |
      | g_qty_in_transit     | "<qty_in_transit>"  |
      | g_qty_mrp_nettable   | "<qty_mrp_net>"     |
      | g_qty_shippable      | "<qty_shippable>"    |

    Examples:
      | item_no_ | location_code | qty_on_hand | qty_allocated | qty_available | qty_fin_net | qty_in_transit | qty_mrp_net | qty_shippable |
      | ITEM009  | HAUPT         | 150.0       | 150.0         | 150.0         | 150.0       | null            | 150.0       | 150.0         |
      | ITEM010  | GERMERING     | 200.0       | 200.0         | 200.0         | 200.0       | null            | 200.0       | 200.0         |
      | ITEM011  | UNKNOWN       | 0.0         | 0.0           | 0.0           | 0.0         | null            | 0.0         | 0.0           |
      | ITEM012  | LIN           | 50.0        | 50.0          | 50.0          | 50.0        | null            | 50.0        | 50.0          |
      | ITEM013  | MATRIUM       | 75.0        | 75.0          | 75.0          | 75.0        | null            | 75.0        | 75.0          |
      | ITEM014  | "AH-001"      | 120.0       | 120.0         | 120.0         | 120.0       | null            | 120.0       | 120.0         |

  Scenario: Handle records with missing or invalid data gracefully
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_          | "ITEM015"                |
      | location_code     | "LOC015"                 |
      | posting_date      | "2023-10-01"              |
      | serial_no_        | "   "                    |
      | lot_no_           | "   "                    |
      | Expiration_Date   | "invalid-date"           |
      | Posting_Date      | "2023-10-01"              |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should have a record with:
      | g_lot_nbr           | "none"                  |
      | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd  | "99991231"              |
      | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd | "99991231"        |
    And an error log should capture:
      | Record_ID | Error_Message                       |
      | ITEM015  | "Invalid Expiration_Date format"    |

  Scenario: Ensure data quality rules are enforced
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | item_no_        | "ITEM016"                |
      | location_code   | "LOC016"                 |
      | posting_date    | "2023-11-01"              |
      | serial_no_      | "SN016"                  |
      | lot_no_         | "LOT016"                 |
      | Expiration_Date | "2024-11-01"              |
      | Posting_Date    | "2023-11-01"              |
      | g_account       | ""                       |
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the SQL logic should enforce data quality:
      | Field      | Rule                          |
      | g_account  | Must be 100% complete          |
    And an error should be raised:
      | Error_Message               | 
      | "g_account is missing"      |

  Scenario: Verify handling of hardcoded fields
    Given a record in itemledgerentrieswopd with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav"                   |
      | g_company_cd     | "1050"                  |
      | g_assignment_type| ""                      |
